(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
In biology there are patterns of life that grow infinitely and uncontrollably \
(such as tumors), other that die out immediately under certain conditions and \
some other that persists for only a finite number of steps. Interestingly, \
some cellular automaton rules exhibit the similar behaviour. This work \
explore such rules within the context  of one-dimensional totalistic cellular \
automata, focusing of those that generate finite life when starting from a \
single cell active.\
\>", "Abstract",
 CellFrame->{{0, 0}, {0, 0.5}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.75],
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.961138517379513*^9},ExpressionUUID->"55d29766-e30b-f34a-8ab3-\
396799777500"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Introduction", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.802186221820878*^9, 3.8021862228082314`*^9}, {
  3.83233589828449*^9, 3.832335898684196*^9}, {3.832335963123202*^9, 
  3.832335974308188*^9}, {3.898169951495221*^9, 3.898169960479115*^9}, {
  3.926610792453679*^9, 3.92661079422296*^9}, {3.9608169660263357`*^9, 
  3.960816969133812*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7aa7184e-d248-af4a-9f4a-\
a226842742ee"],

Cell["\<\
Cellular Automata (CA) are simple mathematical systems that evolve in \
discrete steps, where each cell in a grid updates its state based on a set of \
rules and the states of its neighbours. Despite their simplicity, they can \
produce surprisingly complex behaviour and have been widely studied in areas \
such as mathematics, physics, computer science, and biology.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8021862859717093`*^9, 3.8021862866993*^9}, {
   3.802186780928506*^9, 3.802186861789569*^9}, {3.832335906349555*^9, 
   3.832335909229568*^9}, {3.832336112805627*^9, 3.832336113421673*^9}, 
   3.833031536056086*^9, {3.83303157648634*^9, 3.833031596344939*^9}, {
   3.898170140258331*^9, 3.898170246020052*^9}, 3.926512499894645*^9, {
   3.9266094882344837`*^9, 3.926609510140595*^9}, {3.926676124832939*^9, 
   3.9266761698317223`*^9}, 3.927272873245349*^9, {3.927359833191084*^9, 
   3.9273598516878605`*^9}, {3.927359892523365*^9, 3.927359923929069*^9}, {
   3.927359957458332*^9, 3.927360015778108*^9}, {3.927360367008919*^9, 
   3.927360367335776*^9}, {3.927361130102511*^9, 3.927361130451678*^9}, {
   3.927361316052264*^9, 3.927361316588394*^9}, {3.960736339210099*^9, 
   3.960736341207962*^9}, {3.9608169706737022`*^9, 3.960816970863718*^9}, {
   3.961028586686831*^9, 3.961028594878585*^9}, {3.961028628659333*^9, 
   3.961028638033821*^9}, {3.9611451200984535`*^9, 3.9611451233217316`*^9}},
 CellID->2124053179,ExpressionUUID->"dfe06fea-2619-a846-83b6-6b46e08bbbec"],

Cell["\<\
Among the different types of behaviour that can emerge from cellular \
automata, one especially interesting case is that of finite lifeforms. These \
are patterns that, starting from a single active cell, grow for a certain \
number of steps before stopping completely. They don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t \
disappear instantly, but they also don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t expand forever. \
This behaviour can be compared to some biological processes that are active \
for a limited time, like certain types of cell growth.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8021862859717093`*^9, 3.8021862866993*^9}, {
   3.802186780928506*^9, 3.802186861789569*^9}, {3.832335906349555*^9, 
   3.832335909229568*^9}, {3.832336112805627*^9, 3.832336113421673*^9}, 
   3.833031536056086*^9, {3.83303157648634*^9, 3.833031596344939*^9}, {
   3.898170140258331*^9, 3.898170246020052*^9}, 3.926512499894645*^9, {
   3.9266094882344837`*^9, 3.926609510140595*^9}, {3.926676124832939*^9, 
   3.9266761698317223`*^9}, 3.927272873245349*^9, {3.927359833191084*^9, 
   3.9273598516878605`*^9}, {3.927359892523365*^9, 3.927359923929069*^9}, {
   3.927359957458332*^9, 3.927360015778108*^9}, {3.927360367008919*^9, 
   3.927360367335776*^9}, {3.927361130102511*^9, 3.927361130451678*^9}, {
   3.927361316052264*^9, 3.927361316588394*^9}, {3.960736339210099*^9, 
   3.960736341207962*^9}, {3.9608169706737022`*^9, 3.960816970863718*^9}, {
   3.961028586686831*^9, 3.961028594878585*^9}, {3.961028628659333*^9, 
   3.961028639766029*^9}, {3.961145126138298*^9, 
   3.961145129587164*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0629e5f7-fede-124f-b2c1-\
30f841bb4ccf"],

Cell["\<\
This project explores totalistic cellular automata in one dimension \
\[LongDash] a class where the rules depend only on the total sum of \
neighbouring cell states. Through a series of filters and computational \
tools, we reduce the number of possible rules and identify which ones can \
generate finite lifeforms. We also analyse how these rules relate to each \
other by building graphs that connect similar behaviours.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8021862859717093`*^9, 3.8021862866993*^9}, {
   3.802186780928506*^9, 3.802186861789569*^9}, {3.832335906349555*^9, 
   3.832335909229568*^9}, {3.832336112805627*^9, 3.832336113421673*^9}, 
   3.833031536056086*^9, {3.83303157648634*^9, 3.833031596344939*^9}, {
   3.898170140258331*^9, 3.898170246020052*^9}, 3.926512499894645*^9, {
   3.9266094882344837`*^9, 3.926609510140595*^9}, {3.926676124832939*^9, 
   3.9266761698317223`*^9}, 3.927272873245349*^9, {3.927359833191084*^9, 
   3.9273598516878605`*^9}, {3.927359892523365*^9, 3.927359923929069*^9}, {
   3.927359957458332*^9, 3.927360015778108*^9}, {3.927360367008919*^9, 
   3.927360367335776*^9}, {3.927361130102511*^9, 3.927361130451678*^9}, {
   3.927361316052264*^9, 3.927361316588394*^9}, {3.960736339210099*^9, 
   3.960736341207962*^9}, {3.9608169706737022`*^9, 3.960816970863718*^9}, {
   3.961028586686831*^9, 3.961028594878585*^9}, {3.961028628659333*^9, 
   3.961028641791401*^9}, {3.9611451348124866`*^9, 
   3.9611451444514484`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3933fa7f-bfbd-4647-ba9e-\
0a7062ba0cd4"],

Cell["\<\
Since testing all possible rules is computationally expensive, we also \
designed an algorithm that discovers new rules by applying small changes \
(mutations) to existing ones. This strategy helps to explore the space of \
rules more efficiently and understand the structure behind these finite \
lifeform patterns.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8021862859717093`*^9, 3.8021862866993*^9}, {
   3.802186780928506*^9, 3.802186861789569*^9}, {3.832335906349555*^9, 
   3.832335909229568*^9}, {3.832336112805627*^9, 3.832336113421673*^9}, 
   3.833031536056086*^9, {3.83303157648634*^9, 3.833031596344939*^9}, {
   3.898170140258331*^9, 3.898170246020052*^9}, 3.926512499894645*^9, {
   3.9266094882344837`*^9, 3.926609510140595*^9}, {3.926676124832939*^9, 
   3.9266761698317223`*^9}, 3.927272873245349*^9, {3.927359833191084*^9, 
   3.9273598516878605`*^9}, {3.927359892523365*^9, 3.927359923929069*^9}, {
   3.927359957458332*^9, 3.927360015778108*^9}, {3.927360367008919*^9, 
   3.927360367335776*^9}, {3.927361130102511*^9, 3.927361130451678*^9}, {
   3.927361316052264*^9, 3.927361316588394*^9}, {3.960736339210099*^9, 
   3.960736341207962*^9}, {3.9608169706737022`*^9, 3.960816970863718*^9}, {
   3.961028586686831*^9, 3.961028594878585*^9}, {3.961028628659333*^9, 
   3.961028641321877*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"74226c38-132d-5747-90d3-\
c872cd2d2b43"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Theoretical framework ", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.802186221820878*^9, 3.8021862228082314`*^9}, {
  3.83233589828449*^9, 3.832335898684196*^9}, {3.832335963123202*^9, 
  3.832335974308188*^9}, {3.898169951495221*^9, 3.898169960479115*^9}, {
  3.926610792453679*^9, 3.92661079422296*^9}, {3.9607494657137403`*^9, 
  3.960749478200831*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6c1496a0-f133-d642-9d2a-\
ba952ace7aff"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Definitions", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.898195524720254*^9, 3.898195535561037*^9}, {
  3.915809133258247*^9, 3.91580913399594*^9}, {3.926609367013923*^9, 
  3.926609368821577*^9}, {3.9266094384454327`*^9, 3.926609440005599*^9}, {
  3.960749480472433*^9, 3.9607494866025476`*^9}},
 CellID->163209267,ExpressionUUID->"163c46a9-02e1-844f-b383-6728dc4ac250"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Cellular Automata", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.898195524720254*^9, 3.898195535561037*^9}, {
  3.915809133258247*^9, 3.91580913399594*^9}, {3.926609367013923*^9, 
  3.926609368821577*^9}, {3.9266094384454327`*^9, 3.926609440005599*^9}, {
  3.9272804090252943`*^9, 3.92728043009965*^9}, {3.960749497343897*^9, 
  3.960749499692769*^9}},
 CellID->276637559,ExpressionUUID->"e18fa5da-74db-334a-afec-6ae3f5ef0f58"],

Cell["\<\
Cellular automata (CA) are defined as a collection of cells arranged in a \
regular grid, where each cell updates its value based on the interaction with \
its neighbors. Mathematically, a cellular automaton is described by a 4-tuple:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8021862859717093`*^9, 3.8021862866993*^9}, {
   3.802186780928506*^9, 3.802186861789569*^9}, {3.832335906349555*^9, 
   3.832335909229568*^9}, {3.832336112805627*^9, 3.832336113421673*^9}, 
   3.833031536056086*^9, {3.83303157648634*^9, 3.833031596344939*^9}, {
   3.898170140258331*^9, 3.898170246020052*^9}, 3.926512499894645*^9, {
   3.9266094882344837`*^9, 3.926609510140595*^9}, {3.926676124832939*^9, 
   3.9266761698317223`*^9}, 3.927272873245349*^9, {3.927359833191084*^9, 
   3.9273598516878605`*^9}, {3.927359892523365*^9, 3.927359923929069*^9}, {
   3.927359957458332*^9, 3.927360015778108*^9}, {3.927360367008919*^9, 
   3.927360367335776*^9}, {3.927361130102511*^9, 3.927361130451678*^9}, {
   3.927361316052264*^9, 3.927361316588394*^9}, {3.960736339210099*^9, 
   3.960736341207962*^9}, {3.960749591722993*^9, 3.960749596722069*^9}, {
   3.960749816188888*^9, 3.9607499532534246`*^9}, {3.960750030381544*^9, 
   3.9607500362558727`*^9}},
 CellID->1756276478,ExpressionUUID->"13bf7cce-60b4-ac49-943b-e6df4d32e55f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["L",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ": The dimensional space. It defines the dimensionality of the grid of \
cells. This space is (theoretically) infinite."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9607501035021563`*^9, 
  3.960750149970566*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"fef22948-2fb3-c446-b9e5-\
39053c4a7385"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["S",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ": A finite set of possible states that each cell can assume within the \
assigned space."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9607501035021563`*^9, 
  3.960750165186715*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"17ea5aef-57b4-3f4e-9e38-\
23fbaa5843a6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["N",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ": The neighborhood. It defines the relative positions of the cells that \
make up each cell\[CloseCurlyQuote]s neighborhood. The behavior of each cell \
depends on the states of its neighbors."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9607501035021563`*^9, 
  3.9607501768039503`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e32753f9-7aa2-2a48-822b-\
77359454d361"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["f",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 StyleBox[": ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "The transition function, defined as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["f", "TI"], ":", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
          RowBox[{"[", 
            StyleBox["N", "TI"], "]"}]], "\[Rule]", 
         StyleBox["S", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "$f:S^{[N]} \\to S$", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7f862359-f8a1-a147-9d5d-aa3c45bd368b"],
 ". It determines the next state of each cell based on the states of its \
neighbors. This update occurs simultaneously for all cells at each discrete \
time step."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9607501035021563`*^9, 
  3.9607503194630833`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c1d2723c-e2cc-5f41-af3b-\
8e55b0abbbf7"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Elementary Cellular Automata", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.898195524720254*^9, 3.898195535561037*^9}, {
  3.915809133258247*^9, 3.91580913399594*^9}, {3.926609367013923*^9, 
  3.926609368821577*^9}, {3.9266094384454327`*^9, 3.926609440005599*^9}, {
  3.9272804090252943`*^9, 3.92728043009965*^9}, {3.960749497343897*^9, 
  3.960749499692769*^9}, {3.960750381087145*^9, 3.960750383474203*^9}, {
  3.960750715016591*^9, 3.96075071517864*^9}},
 CellID->1476953314,ExpressionUUID->"3785d19e-ed79-ac4e-aeef-b4bdfd6ea88b"],

Cell["\<\
Elementary Cellular Automata (ECA) represent the simplest class of cellular \
automata. Their characteristics are as follows:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8021862859717093`*^9, 3.8021862866993*^9}, {
   3.802186780928506*^9, 3.802186861789569*^9}, {3.832335906349555*^9, 
   3.832335909229568*^9}, {3.832336112805627*^9, 3.832336113421673*^9}, 
   3.833031536056086*^9, {3.83303157648634*^9, 3.833031596344939*^9}, {
   3.898170140258331*^9, 3.898170246020052*^9}, 3.926512499894645*^9, {
   3.9266094882344837`*^9, 3.926609510140595*^9}, {3.926676124832939*^9, 
   3.9266761698317223`*^9}, 3.927272873245349*^9, {3.927359833191084*^9, 
   3.9273598516878605`*^9}, {3.927359892523365*^9, 3.927359923929069*^9}, {
   3.927359957458332*^9, 3.927360015778108*^9}, {3.927360367008919*^9, 
   3.927360367335776*^9}, {3.927361130102511*^9, 3.927361130451678*^9}, {
   3.927361316052264*^9, 3.927361316588394*^9}, {3.960736339210099*^9, 
   3.960736341207962*^9}, {3.960749591722993*^9, 3.960749596722069*^9}, {
   3.960749816188888*^9, 3.9607499532534246`*^9}, {3.960750030381544*^9, 
   3.9607500362558727`*^9}, {3.960750439563765*^9, 3.960750475274056*^9}, {
   3.960750507621759*^9, 3.9607505134126062`*^9}, {3.9607514237054157`*^9, 
   3.960751425364295*^9}},
 CellID->727504580,ExpressionUUID->"25dacf8d-ad9a-3e46-86bd-cb21d23da6cb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["L = 1",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ": The cell are arranged in a  one-dimensional consecutive infinite line. "
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9607501035021563`*^9, 3.960750149970566*^9}, {
  3.960750535749392*^9, 3.960750579933288*^9}, {3.960751432440866*^9, 
  3.960751444461165*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c3183e04-6d0b-954d-9156-\
b359b75d6f6d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["S = {0, 1}",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ": Each cell can be in one of two possible states."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9607501035021563`*^9, 3.960750165186715*^9}, {
  3.960750587429061*^9, 3.960750605250572*^9}, {3.960751458948997*^9, 
  3.9607514593484383`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"89122607-2dcf-fe44-a7f9-\
365669371376"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["N = {-1, 0, 1}",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ": The neighborhood consists of the cell itself and its two immediate \
neighbors, one to the left and one to the right. This is also referred to as \
radius 1."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9607501035021563`*^9, 3.9607503194630833`*^9}, {
  3.9607506785912247`*^9, 3.9607506797695007`*^9}, {3.960751468781991*^9, 
  3.960751480944538*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e753001c-2c42-9847-b96b-\
83b704539a5c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The transition function depends on the states of three cells, and since \
each cell can be in one of two states, there are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox[
          TemplateBox[{
            RowBox[{
              StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]}, "Abs"], 
          TemplateBox[{
            RowBox[{
              StyleBox["N", "TI"]}]}, "Abs"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SuperscriptBox["2", "3"], "\[LongEqual]", "8"}], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "${|S|}^{|N|}=2^3=8$", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "34fa9f5b-517d-6d4b-8f1f-c53a10727e83"],
 " possible neighborhood configurations. Each of these 8 configurations can \
map to either 0 or 1 as the next state, which gives us a total of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          SuperscriptBox[
           TemplateBox[{
             RowBox[{
               StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]}, "Abs"], 
           SuperscriptBox[
            TemplateBox[{
              RowBox[{
                StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]}, "Abs"], 
            TemplateBox[{
              RowBox[{
                StyleBox["N", "TI"]}]}, "Abs"]]], "\[LongEqual]", 
          SuperscriptBox["2", 
           SuperscriptBox["2", "3"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
          SuperscriptBox["2", "8"], "\[LongEqual]", "256"}], TraditionalForm],
       "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "${|S|}^{{|S|}^{|N|}}=2^{2^3}=2^8=256$", 
      "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
     "TeXAssistantTemplate"], " "}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ec564bd7-81ac-ef45-bf8a-cb77547540f3"],
 " different elementary cellular automaton rules."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9607501035021563`*^9, 3.9607503194630833`*^9}, {
  3.9607506785912247`*^9, 3.960750801665948*^9}, {3.960750909750814*^9, 
  3.960751019179801*^9}, {3.960751784780629*^9, 3.960751808406002*^9}, {
  3.96075187466147*^9, 
  3.960751878268414*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"303a0e7e-9b4a-f147-b03e-\
a05046a516e9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each rule can be uniquely identified by the binary output assigned to the 8 \
neighborhood configurations. This binary number can be interpreted as a \
decimal value between 0 and 255. For example, the rule corresponding to the \
binary sequence ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "11010010"], "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "fbdcf704-a7ba-814f-9f41-366d8dd0f986"],
 " is known as ",
 StyleBox["Rule 210",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", since  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["210", "10"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SubscriptBox["11010010", "2"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "210_{10}=11010010_2", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "1f42b5e7-511e-9f47-958c-056374ff5e81"],
 "."
}], "Text",
