Cell["\<\
The 3D plot below displays all discovered rules under 700 steps for the same \
configuration.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.961019548829008*^9, 3.9610196638449078`*^9}, {
  3.961019773627499*^9, 3.961019778892055*^9}, {3.9610198157468777`*^9, 
  3.961020012458035*^9}, {3.961020097700416*^9, 3.9610201054168453`*^9}, {
  3.9611453376387386`*^9, 
  3.9611453379085846`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"53e2f821-6b5b-6b4f-a9c7-\
636f6bc808e1"],

Cell["\<\
The height of each node represents the scaled length of the lifeform.\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96102011295469*^9, 
  3.961020113838353*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"dbb66022-3ed2-ea4d-9c18-\
94b33a2f3253"],

Cell["\<\
Edges indicate that one rule can be transformed into another via a single \
mutation in the rule vector.\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96102011295469*^9, 
  3.961020118318815*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5fd5fa76-85ba-654d-9b71-\
0db25af10e02"],

Cell["\<\
A common pattern observed across all graphs is that longer lifeforms tend to \
have fewer connections . This sparsity in connectivity makes random walks a \
poor strategy for discovering long finite lifeforms, as the probability of \
reaching high-scoring configurations becomes significantly lower.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.961020122440673*^9, 3.961020133736541*^9}, 
   3.961020172413656*^9},ExpressionUUID->"27359a81-9f8d-2940-9fd9-\
4a3c82a94236"],

